### What is the Facade pattern?

A subsystem often grows into many collaborating classes, each doing part of a workflow. If every client has to know all those classes and the right sequence, the client becomes tightly coupled to the subsystem. The facade solves this by exposing a small number of coarse-grained methods that represent what clients actually want to do.

### How does delegation work inside a facade?

The facade holds references to subsystem classes and calls them in the correct order.

```java
package com.bank.facade;

import com.bank.service.CreditScoreService;
import com.bank.service.IncomeVerificationService;
import com.bank.service.PropertyValuationService;
import com.bank.service.LegalTitleService;
import com.bank.service.DisbursementService;
import java.math.BigDecimal;

public class LoanApprovalFacade {

    private final CreditScoreService creditScore;
    private final IncomeVerificationService income;
    private final PropertyValuationService property;
    private final LegalTitleService legal;
    private final DisbursementService disbursement;

    public LoanApprovalFacade(CreditScoreService creditScore,
                              IncomeVerificationService income,
                              PropertyValuationService property,
                              LegalTitleService legal,
                              DisbursementService disbursement) {
        this.creditScore = creditScore;
        this.income = income;
        this.property = property;
        this.legal = legal;
        this.disbursement = disbursement;
    }

    public LoanDecision approveHomeLoan(String customerId, BigDecimal amount) {
        int score = creditScore.fetch(customerId);
        if (score < 700) return LoanDecision.rejected("Credit score below 700");

        boolean incomeOk = income.verify(customerId, amount);
        if (!incomeOk) return LoanDecision.rejected("Income insufficient");

        BigDecimal valuation = property.valuate(customerId);
        boolean titleClear = legal.checkTitle(customerId);
        if (!titleClear) return LoanDecision.rejected("Title not clear");

        disbursement.disburse(customerId, amount);
        return LoanDecision.approved(amount, valuation);
    }
}
```

